 "lines": [
  [
   "hook",
   "In 1917, America paid Denmark twenty-five million dollars in gold for a few Caribbean islands."
  ],
  [
   "ask",
   "So why did America want them so badly?"
  ],
  [
   "canal",
   "Because they sit near the sea routes to the Panama Canal, which had just opened in 1914."
  ],
  [
   "war",
   "And in World War One, America feared Germany could take control of them."
  ],
  [
   "push",
   "So it told Denmark it would never allow that, and Denmark agreed to sell."
  ],
  [
   "deal",
   "On March 31st, 1917, the islands became the U.S. Virgin Islands."
  ],
  [
   "today",
   "Every year, residents still mark that day as Transfer Day."
  ],
  [
   "end",
   "Gold coins and a fear of Germany turned Danish islands into American ones. That's the map answer."
  ]
 ],
